 "whole_interface_source": "Displacing the TRUE target chain of 9DTY.cif by 32.0 A rigid RMSD drops DockQ to a median of 0.025 \u2014 at or below the best of our 12 co-folds (0.023-0.046). So the co-folds are not a near-miss on placement: they score like the correct structure moved 32 A.",
 "worst_half_rmsd_A": 3.192,
 "ratio_whole_to_worst_half": 10.0,
 "failure_locus": "assembly",
 "sentence": "All 12 co-folds place the degrader within 3.2 A of its crystal position in EACH protein's own frame (target median 1.83 A, E3 median 1.95 A), while the assembled interface scores what the TRUE complex scores when displaced 32 A \u2014 a factor of 10. The halves are approximately right and the ASSEMBLY of them is wrong, so the missing information is the relative placement of the two proteins: exactly what a ternary generator is given when it is handed each end's site."
}